:17,"finishRateRank":69,"winningTimeRank":17,"winningTimeRankDir":12,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1974,"mensWinner":"Derek PREISS","mensTime":"06:02:49"}},"narrative":"The 1997 Comrades Marathon was the 72nd running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.900 km. The race was held on Monday, 16 June. Conditions: Chilly morning, mild to warm later. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nCharl MATTHEUS claimed the men's title in 05:28:37, ahead of Nick BESTER (05:30:41) and Jaroslaw JANICKI (05:32:50). Ann TRASON won the women's race in 05:58:25, followed by Maria BAK (06:00:28).\n\nAnn TRASON's 05:58:25 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1974 (Derek PREISS, 06:02:49).\n\nFrom a field of 13,831 entries, 11,352 runners crossed the finish line (82.1% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,985 men and 1,367 women (12.0% female). The average finish time was 09:35:50.\n\nMedals awarded: 15 Gold, 921 Silver, 10,416 Bronze. 2,655 runners (23.4%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Steven DOUGLAS in 10:59:59.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 37% of the finishers, with 7,194 seniors (avg 09:29:06) and 4,158 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}